WEBVTT

00:03.440 --> 00:04.560
Why...?

00:10.320 --> 00:12.660
Why did things end up like this?

00:18.330 --> 00:19.500
Am I...?

00:20.790 --> 00:22.250
Am I already...?

00:30.840 --> 00:39.610
(Wanting you to just be near,
to feel your breath upon my ear)

00:39.650 --> 00:48.650
(Wishing you would call my name,
'Cause only you can light the flame)

00:48.690 --> 00:55.420
Constantly searching,
still can't find

00:58.030 --> 01:04.100
Ever illusive peace of mind

01:06.270 --> 01:14.840
Sometimes it's near,
but slips away

01:14.880 --> 01:21.480
And I'm faced with another day

01:22.690 --> 01:28.420
Of wanting you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:28.460 --> 01:32.760
...to just be near
('Cause only you can light the flame)

01:32.800 --> 01:37.240
Of wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:37.270 --> 01:41.670
...would call my name,
to feel your breath upon my ear

01:41.710 --> 01:46.200
Of wanting you... wishing you...
(to feel your breath upon my ear)

01:46.250 --> 01:54.090
Call my name, 'cause only
you can light the flame

01:59.230 --> 02:03.480
HAKUZOUSOU

02:04.650 --> 02:05.570
Umm...

02:05.910 --> 02:07.360
are we almost across?

02:10.660 --> 02:11.910
Jeez...

02:11.910 --> 02:14.370
I just wanted to gather some more
material for one of my 100 stories...

02:18.540 --> 02:20.710
That eye again?

02:30.680 --> 02:32.680
He has retired, you know?

02:32.680 --> 02:33.930
How awful.

02:34.060 --> 02:35.640
What if he hears us?

02:37.690 --> 02:40.690
I don't care if he hears us, that loser.

02:40.820 --> 02:44.400
That's right. He's young and he still doesn't work.

02:44.860 --> 02:46.950
Seriously. He'll never amount to anything.

02:48.200 --> 02:49.950
Amount to something?

02:53.200 --> 02:54.950
This won't amount to anything.

03:00.750 --> 03:01.750
How can that be?!

03:01.750 --> 03:03.300
I tried very hard on that!

03:07.010 --> 03:10.010
Perhaps you just aren't meant to write children's riddles.

03:11.180 --> 03:12.390
How can that be?

03:12.390 --> 03:16.060
Well, do you have your 100 stories, sensei?

03:16.270 --> 03:18.730
I, umm... well...

03:19.650 --> 03:22.020
When it's done, I'll come by to take a look.

03:22.610 --> 03:26.360
Of course, that's only if you finish while I'm still alive.

03:38.710 --> 03:40.290
I don't like this sky...

03:47.130 --> 03:48.170
You're...!

03:49.680 --> 03:52.640
I came here because he said he
had a good kaidan to tell me,

03:52.890 --> 03:54.850
but I wonder if it was a mistake to come...

04:19.750 --> 04:22.670
Y-You can help me if you want!

04:23.340 --> 04:27.250
It's said that before people die, they see their entire lives
flash before them as if they were
watching a revolving lantern.

04:27.550 --> 04:29.670
What did you see, sensei?

04:30.470 --> 04:32.760
I-Im alive!

04:32.760 --> 04:34.180
Please don't say strange things like that.

04:38.310 --> 04:41.440
The first time we met, you saved me, right?

04:43.440 --> 04:44.480
Why was that?

04:45.980 --> 04:48.690
It was just a whim, perhaps.

04:50.860 --> 04:54.660
Are you saying that I'm only alive because of a whim?

04:54.990 --> 04:56.830
I would expect as much from an author.

04:57.120 --> 04:58.870
You say the most Interesting things.

05:00.500 --> 05:01.460
A revolving lantern...

05:02.540 --> 05:04.210
I don't see anything.

05:04.580 --> 05:08.710
I don't have anything worth seeing.

05:09.010 --> 05:09.920
Nothing at all...

05:14.760 --> 05:16.100
Why?

05:16.890 --> 05:18.100
Why did it happen?

05:18.640 --> 05:22.060
How does it justify the fact that I've been killing people?

05:26.190 --> 05:27.670
Izou

05:26.190 --> 05:27.670
Bandit

05:29.070 --> 05:30.230
Boss!

05:31.320 --> 05:33.990
Perhaps because there were many kitsune in this area,

05:34.110 --> 05:37.280
[Note: Kitsune are foxes. They were thought to be magical animals.]

05:34.270 --> 05:37.390
the legend of Hakuzousu came to be associated
with the temple that we passed, Houtouji.

05:37.910 --> 05:40.620
Hakuzousu? That's strange.

05:40.910 --> 05:44.160
[Note: Kai was one of the nations.]

05:40.910 --> 05:44.160
I was sure Hakuzousu was a legend of Kai.

05:46.210 --> 05:47.750
You are indeed knowledgeable.

05:48.090 --> 05:51.210
Would you tell me of this legend?

05:51.920 --> 05:58.550
[Note: Bakegitsune is a kitsune that can change shape.]

05:51.920 --> 05:58.550
Yes. It is said that an ancient Bakegitsune
used to live on Mt. Yume in Kai.

05:59.680 --> 06:02.520
That Bakegitsune had many children,

06:03.100 --> 06:08.440
but all of them except one were
caught by hunters and killed.

06:09.110 --> 06:13.320
The hunter had an uncle named Hakuzousu
who was a Buddhist priest.

06:14.570 --> 06:17.200
The Bakegitsune took Hakuzousu's shape,

06:17.450 --> 06:20.490
and warned the hunter that if he continued to kill,

06:20.490 --> 06:22.240
then he would be unable to enter paradise.

06:22.990 --> 06:25.310
The Bakegitsune then gave the hunter
money to stop killing kitsune;

06:26.420 --> 06:31.300
however, after the hunter spent all of the money
he tried to demand more from Hakuzousu.

06:32.270 --> 06:35.460
Upon hearing of this, the Bakegitsune killed the priest,

06:35.680 --> 06:39.930
took his form, and stayed in the temple.

06:41.100 --> 06:42.930
One day, after fifty years had passed,

06:43.060 --> 06:45.230
The Bakegitsune, in Hakuzousu's form,
left the temple to watch a deer hunt.

06:45.230 --> 06:46.440
Some dogs caught his scent

06:47.060 --> 06:48.940
and he was devoured.

06:50.440 --> 06:51.730
I see.

06:51.900 --> 06:54.940
However, Houtouji's Hakuzousu still lives.

06:55.570 --> 06:57.700
Hakuzousu is alive?

06:58.240 --> 07:00.910
Furthermore, the hunter, Yasaku,

07:00.910 --> 07:02.790
didn't kill just kitsune.

07:02.790 --> 07:06.290
He also began killing people toward the end.

07:07.830 --> 07:09.080
Please wait!

07:10.090 --> 07:11.420
Just what are you...

07:12.050 --> 07:14.590
That hunter, Yasaku... You can't possibly be planning to...

07:15.260 --> 07:19.340
[Note: Youkai is a synonym for mononoke.]

07:15.260 --> 07:19.340
What I am going to do is youkai
extermination, pure and simple.

07:19.760 --> 07:20.930
Youkai?

07:21.550 --> 07:24.890
Are you saying that that Enkai-san, the Buddhist
priest, and Kichibe-san were both youkai?

07:25.480 --> 07:28.390
After all, they possessed an inhuman darkness.

07:29.190 --> 07:31.110
So that is why you killed them?

07:31.230 --> 07:35.480
The one I'm after this time is just a little hit worse though.

07:35.820 --> 07:37.400
After all, not only does Yasaku lack that inhuman darkness,

07:38.110 --> 07:40.160
but he also feels no guilt.

07:42.950 --> 07:45.740
Kill them! Kill them all!

07:49.710 --> 07:53.040
I'm sorry,... but the boss ordered it...

07:53.040 --> 07:55.670
If I disobey him, then he will kill me too.

07:55.840 --> 07:56.920
So...?

08:02.010 --> 08:05.720
So, he transfers the guilt from his crimes
to others while he enjoys killing?

08:05.720 --> 08:06.770
Yes.

08:07.020 --> 08:10.640
In the end, he even kills his fiancée, Towa.

08:11.100 --> 08:13.110
But you people are two of the same.

08:13.730 --> 08:16.150
What you're doing is simply murder!

08:16.690 --> 08:20.110
I didn't think you'd understand.

08:21.610 --> 08:24.660
Y-You can't... you can't intend to kill me, too?!

08:25.950 --> 08:28.660
If you tell anybody about us, then yes.

08:33.130 --> 08:37.500
Is that why you brought me out here?

08:37.510 --> 08:38.960
I'm just making a request.

08:39.720 --> 08:40.720
I-I'm going home!

08:42.930 --> 08:44.600
What are you trying to do?

08:48.850 --> 08:50.640
Just what it looks like.

08:50.640 --> 08:53.500
Jeez... If that's all you wanted to do, then
why did you bring him out here?

08:56.070 --> 08:58.900
Could it be that Kyougokutei...

09:05.620 --> 09:08.450
The weather has been quite fine lately.

09:08.450 --> 09:09.700
Indeed.

09:11.750 --> 09:15.920
Now that I think about it, what happened to that
young man who was a writer of some sort?

09:15.920 --> 09:18.300
Wasn't his name "Momosuke"?

09:18.300 --> 09:21.510
That's right! Momo-chan, Momosuke-chan, wasn't it?

09:21.510 --> 09:26.470
Writers try to spread what they know to the entire
world as quickly as they can, don't they?

09:26.470 --> 09:28.310
That could be bad!

09:29.060 --> 09:32.140
You'd better shut him up fast, shouldn't you?

09:32.140 --> 09:34.060
Yes, shouldn't you?

09:34.980 --> 09:35.940
Kill him.

09:36.190 --> 09:40.360
Or, if he looks to be useful, then the Master can...

09:40.070 --> 09:42.070
The Master can...!

09:42.070 --> 09:44.410
Umm... I'll pass.

09:44.660 --> 09:48.910
I'm sorry to keep making impossible requests of you.

09:50.700 --> 09:52.410
How troublesome.

09:52.410 --> 09:53.580
It always is.

09:55.040 --> 09:57.960
Then was it okay to let him go?

09:58.500 --> 10:00.960
So what? Even if I tried to...

10:01.550 --> 10:02.970
I see...

10:05.010 --> 10:08.140
Jeez... why is this happening to me?

10:10.390 --> 10:13.140
My legs feel like sticks!

10:13.730 --> 10:16.650
I can't write my 100 stories if this sort
of thing keeps happening to me.

10:21.110 --> 10:22.280
A hunter?

10:25.740 --> 10:26.700
Umm...

10:27.320 --> 10:29.160
Are you Yasaku-san?

10:34.960 --> 10:37.620
This person is Yasaku?

10:38.880 --> 10:41.250
You must not go further down this path.

10:41.500 --> 10:44.130
Have we met somewhere before?

10:44.800 --> 10:46.130
W-Well...

10:47.380 --> 10:50.640
There are people waiting to kill you up ahead.

10:52.350 --> 10:56.060
I'm sorry to ask, but did you really kill people?

10:57.480 --> 10:58.640
Wh-What are you saying?

10:59.360 --> 11:01.150
I heard that you even killed your fiancée...

11:02.320 --> 11:02.610
How?

11:03.900 --> 11:05.150
Is it true?

11:05.530 --> 11:07.610
How does this guy know?

11:10.120 --> 11:11.120
What's wrong?

11:13.990 --> 11:16.250
Yasaku-san, that way is...

11:26.720 --> 11:27.880
It won't wash off...

11:29.220 --> 11:31.180
Why won't it wash off?

11:35.140 --> 11:37.390
Oh my... excuse me.

11:37.810 --> 11:38.940
Oh, err, don't mind me.

11:43.570 --> 11:44.900
What's wrong?

11:44.900 --> 11:45.360
What?

11:50.280 --> 11:51.610
You have manly hands...

11:51.990 --> 11:53.570
Th-There's blood on them...

11:54.330 --> 11:55.330
Where?

11:55.790 --> 11:56.490
What?!

11:57.500 --> 11:58.450
Why?

11:59.370 --> 12:01.170
Perhaps you were hallucinating?

12:01.880 --> 12:03.000
Hallucinating?

12:03.340 --> 12:05.250
I'm not a hallucination.

12:07.630 --> 12:11.130
It's hard to imagine why a woman as beautiful as
yourself is all the way out here in the mountains.

12:11.680 --> 12:13.720
My, you're good with words.

12:13.800 --> 12:15.850
[Note: Tanuki is raccoon dog. They wore also thought to be magical animals.]

12:13.800 --> 12:15.850
I am neither a tanuki nor a kitsune.

12:17.930 --> 12:20.600
There are no more kitsune around here.

12:21.730 --> 12:22.350
Why?

12:23.230 --> 12:25.190
I killed them all.

12:25.400 --> 12:26.940
Are you a hunter?

12:27.110 --> 12:30.150
Well, well. You're stronger than you look then.

12:30.490 --> 12:32.860
I like my men like that.

12:35.080 --> 12:37.080
I'll go with you.

12:37.790 --> 12:40.250
So let's run away together.

12:40.960 --> 12:42.790
You're a kind person.

12:43.380 --> 12:47.710
You told me that you could hunt kitsune in this
forest and that we could live together forever.

12:50.340 --> 12:51.090
Towa!

12:51.510 --> 12:53.890
I know everything.

12:54.510 --> 12:57.350
Even that you're being used by the bandit, Izou,...

12:59.060 --> 13:00.310
but I don't care.

13:00.890 --> 13:03.020
So let's run away together.

13:03.060 --> 13:05.310
Let's live quietly somewhere in the countryside.

13:05.980 --> 13:06.940
But...

13:08.280 --> 13:10.320
I was told by my boss...

13:10.690 --> 13:11.320
Told what?

13:12.030 --> 13:16.070
Anybody who got wind of us... needs to die.

13:22.000 --> 13:24.710
Wh-Why?

13:29.000 --> 13:31.670
I-I'm not the one at fault.

13:32.010 --> 13:33.050
The boss said...

13:36.010 --> 13:37.350
It will be all right.

13:38.220 --> 13:40.010
In a short while, you'll be at peace.

13:42.690 --> 13:44.270
Y-Yasaku-san!

13:52.530 --> 13:53.740
Yasaku-san!

13:58.330 --> 13:59.280
Is everything okay?

13:59.280 --> 14:00.580
What are you talking about?

14:01.160 --> 14:02.000
Let's go.

14:02.160 --> 14:03.710
We'll be better off away from here.

14:05.460 --> 14:08.670
A long time ago, I hunted kitsune in this forest.

14:08.710 --> 14:10.590
That was your job, right?

14:11.380 --> 14:12.670
That's not all.

14:13.050 --> 14:16.680
I was caught in a moment of weakness by the boss
of a gang of bandits, and I even killed people...

14:16.840 --> 14:18.470
If you had disobeyed your orders,

14:18.470 --> 14:19.970
then you would've been the one who was killed, right?

14:20.890 --> 14:22.520
It was to live!

14:22.640 --> 14:24.480
No one will blame you!

14:25.190 --> 14:26.980
Thank you.

14:31.480 --> 14:32.440
Where are you going?

14:33.400 --> 14:36.450
I wanted to enjoy myself a little more.

14:37.070 --> 14:38.990
Jeez, you can't be left alone for even a second.

14:39.160 --> 14:42.910
That sensei came back faster than I thought he would.

14:43.120 --> 14:45.000
He's stupid.

14:45.160 --> 14:47.500
He should've just gone back to Edo.

14:47.830 --> 14:49.710
I don't know about that.

14:49.710 --> 14:50.380
What?

14:50.840 --> 14:52.460
Kyougokutei is in Edo.

14:53.610 --> 14:55.820
I see. If he had returned, then he still would've...

14:56.400 --> 14:58.280
That's about right.

15:06.140 --> 15:07.390
Priest Fugen!

15:08.060 --> 15:10.440
It's me, Yasaku. I'm back.

15:12.730 --> 15:13.730
Dogs?

15:15.530 --> 15:17.400
It seems like there is no one here.

15:19.870 --> 15:20.870
What's wrong?

15:21.200 --> 15:24.160
There are no priests here.

15:25.080 --> 15:26.160
After all,

15:26.830 --> 15:31.420
I killed the priest Fugen ten years ago when he
came to try and stop me from hunting kitsune.

15:31.750 --> 15:32.670
What?

15:33.000 --> 15:37.050
Then Izou used that to blackmail me into joining his band.

15:37.420 --> 15:40.930
Afterwards, Izou cleverly impersonated the priest,

15:41.140 --> 15:44.260
used this temple as his stronghold,
and did whatever he wanted.

15:44.600 --> 15:46.890
But, he was beheaded.

15:47.560 --> 15:50.190
So, I don't have to kill anymore.

15:50.400 --> 15:51.520
I don't have to kill...

15:51.520 --> 15:54.230
You have a convenient way of putting
things, don't you, you little devil?

15:56.110 --> 15:57.490
Boss!

15:57.860 --> 16:00.240
You were threatened by me into killing people, you say?

16:01.320 --> 16:03.950
You love killing.

16:03.950 --> 16:06.240
You have ever since you were a kid, isn't that right?

16:07.910 --> 16:10.460
You're a weak man,

16:10.460 --> 16:12.920
so you tried to believe that you were strong

16:13.040 --> 16:15.840
by killing insects and animals that were defenseless.

16:16.460 --> 16:20.170
You became addicted to the pleasure of taking life!

16:20.180 --> 16:21.180
That's not true...

16:21.970 --> 16:25.430
You wanted to kill. You wanted to feel good.

16:25.600 --> 16:27.640
So, you kept killing.

16:27.770 --> 16:28.600
No!

16:28.600 --> 16:31.140
When you could've run away with Towa,

16:31.190 --> 16:35.980
you deliberately chose the path of being
a murderer and then blamed it on me!

16:36.150 --> 16:36.820
No!

16:36.820 --> 16:38.530
You're a murderer!

16:38.530 --> 16:41.450
A villain who likes killing others.

16:42.240 --> 16:43.320
Strange...

16:43.740 --> 16:45.950
something's strange about this Izou character.

16:46.620 --> 16:48.870
Even if he was Yasaku-san's boss,

16:48.870 --> 16:50.960
why would he know about Yasaku-san's childhood?

16:51.580 --> 16:54.250
Houtouji's Hakuzousu yet lives.

16:56.380 --> 16:58.340
Is that right? He's the Hakuzousu!

16:59.090 --> 17:01.470
This person isn't Izou!

17:01.550 --> 17:02.630
He's a kitsune!

17:03.140 --> 17:04.340
Now, quickly!

17:05.430 --> 17:06.550
Wait!

17:07.390 --> 17:10.060
If he is the Hakuzousu, then he shouldn't
be able to deal with dogs!

17:28.290 --> 17:31.040
This may all have been a kitsunes trickery...

17:32.670 --> 17:36.580
Then I was always... by a kitsune...

17:37.670 --> 17:38.590
Let's go...

17:38.840 --> 17:41.590
We need to get away from here as soon as possible.

17:45.720 --> 17:46.680
Jeez.

17:49.220 --> 17:53.940
[Note: Mata no Ji is Mataichi's nickname.]

17:49.220 --> 17:53.940
I hadn't heard that the writer sensei
would be coming along, Mata no Ji.

18:03.820 --> 18:05.450
Don't look, we'll go around.

18:08.660 --> 18:10.120
Take me... with you.

18:10.700 --> 18:11.950
Help...

18:15.210 --> 18:15.710
Don't look!

18:38.900 --> 18:40.110
Yasaku-san.

18:41.650 --> 18:43.440
H-Help me! Yasaku-san.

18:44.450 --> 18:46.200
This is the end for you.

18:48.160 --> 18:50.530
This saves me the trouble of killing you.

18:50.740 --> 18:54.830
I can't let you live now that you know my true nature.

18:55.750 --> 18:56.620
B-But, that's...

18:56.670 --> 18:59.290
I'll give you a parting gift and tell you something interesting.

18:59.750 --> 19:02.250
What Hakuzousu said was true.

19:02.340 --> 19:04.960
I love killing people.

19:05.170 --> 19:08.970
I love watching their faces as they die.

19:09.300 --> 19:11.720
You're an idiot!

19:19.230 --> 19:20.310
L-Let go!

19:23.190 --> 19:24.980
S-Save me!

19:28.950 --> 19:32.580
If I let go, then he'll survive, but...

19:33.120 --> 19:36.660
If you save me, then I'll repay you with
money for the rest of your life...

19:36.660 --> 19:37.540
So please,

19:37.540 --> 19:39.500
this person has lived desperately...

19:40.080 --> 19:41.330
far more so than I.

19:41.840 --> 19:44.550
I won't lie anymore!

19:45.300 --> 19:46.260
Ever?

19:46.800 --> 19:49.800
Never! I'll never kill anyone again!

20:04.780 --> 20:06.030
I'm saved.

20:06.150 --> 20:07.610
What an idiot.

20:07.990 --> 20:09.530
Weren't you saved thanks to that idiot?

20:10.280 --> 20:12.030
If you insist on maintaining your own Way,

20:15.040 --> 20:17.040
then you will aggravate people,

20:17.620 --> 20:20.250
but if you stray from your ethics,
then you will fall into depravity.

20:20.620 --> 20:23.040
Evil and ambition scatter into the darkness

20:23.040 --> 20:25.750
and all that remains is a dubious
rumor among the townsfolk.

20:26.380 --> 20:27.880
Wh-Who are you people?

20:28.130 --> 20:30.510
Are you friends of that idiot?

20:30.970 --> 20:33.510
I-It's useless to preach to me.

20:33.970 --> 20:35.720
I'm not afraid of anything anymore!

20:35.760 --> 20:36.760
No matter how many animals...

20:37.270 --> 20:38.270
or people I may kill!

20:49.030 --> 20:51.530
I will not let you die so easily.

20:55.950 --> 21:01.370
You will suffer for the length of
all the lives that you've taken.

21:11.090 --> 21:14.430
Why did things end up like this?

21:15.760 --> 21:17.680
This is the end for me.

21:18.890 --> 21:21.140
That revolving lantern didn't show up after all.

21:21.890 --> 21:25.610
My life was nothing special.

21:28.030 --> 21:29.940
Have I died?

21:30.860 --> 21:35.110
Yasaku-san wasn't the only one those guys were after.

21:36.080 --> 21:38.530
They were also after me.

21:39.500 --> 21:41.870
This peaceful feeling...

21:42.370 --> 21:44.580
I've never felt it before.

21:47.920 --> 21:50.090
I can't believe this guy's kindness!

21:52.420 --> 21:56.430
After disobeying Kyougokutei,
how do you intend to live?

21:56.550 --> 22:00.260
If you're worried about that, then why don't
you just go back by yourself, Ogin-san?

22:00.850 --> 22:03.180
It's up to me where I go.

22:15.780 --> 22:21.870
Wind chimes whisper
soft and sweet

22:23.220 --> 22:29.310
Though there's not
a hint of a breeze

22:30.290 --> 22:36.060
Moonlight dancing
on the garden walk

22:36.100 --> 22:42.730
As it gently drifts
through the trees

22:44.100 --> 22:50.040
Romance takes flight
on this perfect night

22:50.080 --> 22:56.740
While all of the world
lays sleeping

22:57.580 --> 23:07.050
Find us here as we feel
the moment of love

23:08.360 --> 23:11.560
Draw near

23:11.830 --> 23:18.830
Dream, sleep,
with your hand in mine

23:18.870 --> 23:24.810
Underneath a blanket of stars

23:26.980 --> 23:32.250
Song birds singing
in a distant glade

23:32.290 --> 23:40.920
As we share
the warmth of the dawn

23:51.800 --> 23:54.050
Evil and ambition scatter into the darkness

23:54.050 --> 23:57.010
and all that remains is a dubious
rumor among the townsfolk.

23:57.930 --> 24:00.140
Women tend to be like a flower;

24:00.350 --> 24:02.350
seductively beautiful and fragrant.

24:02.810 --> 24:04.890
Is this a female's karma?

24:05.310 --> 24:07.640
What blossoms in Oyoshi's heart?

24:08.060 --> 24:12.520
On the next Kyougoku Natsuhiko's
Rumors: Hundred Stories,

24:12.820 --> 24:13.980
Maikubi.

24:14.530 --> 24:17.110
The deed is done.
